                <note rend="inline" type="source">882.51/1345b: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to
                        the Minister in Liberia</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                            >Johnson</hi>)</head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1921-11-14T13:00:00-05:00"><hi rendition="#italic">November 14,
                                1921—1 p.m.</hi></date></dateline></opener>
                <p>28. President King and other members of the Plenary Commission are returning to
                    Liberia sailing November 15th from Boston on U.S.S. <hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Denver</hi> in command of Captain Kautz. The cruiser has been detailed for
                    this purpose by United States Government and should be about 16 days <hi
                        rendition="#italic">en route</hi>. You may make this public.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Hughes</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
